\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Two-stage verification architecture for the canonical VQE instance. The contract families retain heterogeneous verification objects. The frozen record precedes execution; runtime checking combines run-level logical/numeric evidence with probabilistic evidence across repeated executions. The displayed verdict names match the implementation. A probabilistic disagreement denotes a model discrepancy only when assumptions and the statistical decision rule justify that interpretation. The architecture supplies traceability rather than an equivalence among NuXmv, Dafny, and Storm.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{3}{Two-stage verification architecture for the canonical VQE instance. The contract families retain heterogeneous verification objects. The frozen record precedes execution; runtime checking combines run-level logical/numeric evidence with probabilistic evidence across repeated executions. The displayed verdict names match the implementation. A probabilistic disagreement denotes a model discrepancy only when assumptions and the statistical decision rule justify that interpretation. The architecture supplies traceability rather than an equivalence among NuXmv, Dafny, and Storm}{figure.1}{}}
